// BUILD01 Final Contract v1
// Build is an emergent, versioned, registry-driven life path. Current v1 counts are manifest facts, never Core limits.
type BuildAffinity={buildId:string;affinityBps:number;lifetimeEvidence:number;lastEvidenceNodeIndex:number};
type BuildStage='latent'|'emerging'|'formed'|'refined';
type BuildDefinition={id:string;displayName:string;familyTags:string[];tags:string[];stages:BuildStageDefinition[];modifiers:BuildModifier[];hooks:BuildHook[];requiresTags:string[];forbidsTags:string[];compatibleWith:string[];conflictsWith:string[];parentBuildIds:string[];unlockConditions?:BuildConditionExpr[];focusPressureBpsByBuildId?:Record<string,number>;systemOwners:string[]};
BuildRules v1 stage ranges are latent 0..1999, emerging 2000..4499, formed 4500..7499, refined 7500..10000.
ADD_BUILD_EVIDENCE is the only BUILD01 Event effect. amount is authoritative safe integer 200..3000 and requires buildId, reasonTag and source trace. Action names and node count never create Evidence.
affinityBps is 0..10000 and may rise or fall. lifetimeEvidence is safe-integer monotonic. Stage is derived and never stored separately.
Positive Evidence X applies versioned focus pressure to other existing affinities: roundHalfUpPositive(X*pairOrDefaultPressureBps,10000), floored at zero. v1 default is 2000 bps.
The first formed Build may become dominant. A challenger switches dominance only at current affinity + versioned margin; v1 margin is 500. Ties use stable buildId ordering and no RNG.
Branch/hybrid unlock uses parentBuildIds plus whitelist BuildConditionExpr. No eval, Function, script strings or arbitrary state paths.
Definition modifiers feed existing PROG01/RISK01 canonical aggregators. Core never switches on sword/body/alchemy/fortune IDs. Fortune has no BUILD01 RNG, Check or Outcome modifier.
Structured facts cover first evidence, stage transition, dominant formed/changed, refined and branch/hybrid unlock with source, command, age, nodeIndex and reasonTag.
Director receives a read-only stage/tag/recent-fact projection. BUILD01 never controls candidate weights, cadence or story generation and never calls AI/network.
Build state is authoritative Snapshot/Replay/hash data locked by rulesVersion+contentVersion. Definitions use stable IDs, tags, registries and whitelist hooks; new Build counts do not require Core changes.